      \field{abstract}{This monograph attempts a new approach for testing construction in psychology. A probabilistic model is developed for 3 different types of tests. Each model implies 2 types of parameters: a "difficulty" for each test or item and an "ability" for each person, independent of which set of tests or items has been employed. Both parameters are estimated from the data. Chapters 1-7 present the basic theory with a minimum of mathematics. Chapters 8-10 present in detail the mathematics underlying the models. From Psyc Abstracts 36:05:5HB84R. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)}
